<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh aircraft skids off runway.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh aircraft skids off runway.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A passenger aircraft of the state-owned airline Bangladesh Biman skidded off the runway while landing amid heavy rain in southern Chittagong, airline officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The 70-seat ATP plane slipped about 50 feet (15 metres) off the runway on to marshland on Wednesday night as the pilot lost visibility due to heavy rain, they said.</p>
<p>Several of the 60 passengers sustained minor injuries.</p>
<p>Officials said they had yet to salvage the plane because of heavy rain.</p>
</text>
